{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":494390,"name":"Francesco Beomonte Zobel","username":"Francesco_Beomonte_Z","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/f/53a042/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T21:50:30.528Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494390-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494390-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494390-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494390-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSince around 15:44 CEST on 17 September my Grok Bot has stopped replying. Every message to every bot fails, and it fails from the phone app as well, so this doesn’t look like something on my machine.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOperating system: macOS 26.6.2, Apple Silicon\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVersion: Grok Bot 0.56.1. It was already happening on 0.55.0, and updating did not change anything.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSteps to reproduce:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSend any message to any bot (mine are Chief and Vinted)\u003cbr\u003e\nStart a brand new chat with an existing bot and send “test”\u003cbr\u003e\nSame thing from the phone app\u003cbr\u003e\nWhat happens: on 0.55.0 the chat showed “Il Bot non ha risposto / Si è verificato un errore durante la generazione della risposta”. After updating to 0.56.1 the error banner no longer appears, the message is simply sent and no reply ever comes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExpected behavior: the bot replies.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat I already tried, with no effect: quitting and reopening the app, updating 0.55.0 to 0.56.1, a new chat, the phone app.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat I deliberately did not try: Reset Agent Computer, Update Agent Computer, reinstalling. Other threads here say staff advise against them in this state and that Reset can delete bots.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLocal log. ~/.grokbot/local-exec-daemon.log contains one line repeated 146 times:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e[user-computer-provider] watch stream failed: ConnectError\u003cbr\u003e\nplus some “poll failed: DeadlineExceededError (deadline_exceeded)” and one ECONNRESET.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eChecks on my side that came back clean: DNS for cursor.sh resolves against both 1.1.1.1 and 8.8.8.8; the certificate for api2.cursor.sh is issued by Amazon RSA 2048 M01, so nothing is intercepting the traffic; weekly usage is at 0%, so it isn’t a quota limit; no crash reports, and the app shows the account as signed in.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis reads like the stuck box described in “Grok Bot stuck: Bot failed to respond on every message, all bots”, which was recovered server side. Could someone check mine?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI don’t have a request ID: the error banner disappeared when the app restarted after the update.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI also emailed \u003ca href=\"mailto:hi@cursor.com\"\u003ehi@cursor.com\u003c/a\u003e with the same details.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494390-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494390-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003esee above\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494390-operating-system-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494390-operating-system-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eiOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494390-version-information-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494390-version-information-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot 0.56.1 (macOS desktop app) — also reproduced on 0.55.0 before updating.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNot working also on my iphone\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494390-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494390-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes - Cursor is unusable\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-17T22:22:37.236Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":18,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":91.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":172074,"topic_slug":"bot-failed-to-respond-on-every-bot-desktop-and-phone-since-15-44-cest-17-sep","display_username":"Francesco Beomonte Zobel","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":138523,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/bot-failed-to-respond-on-every-bot-desktop-and-phone-since-15-44-cest-17-sep/172074/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":494395,"name":"Landon Taylor","username":"Landon_Taylor","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/ed655f/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-17T22:10:31.680Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eSame for me\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-17T22:10:31.680Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_lin